course: dictionary
lesson: 10507
title: One word, two meanings: twig
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A twig is a small, thin branch of a tree or bush. Trees have a trunk, branches grow from the trunk, and smaller twigs grow from the branches. Twig is a noun, so you can say a twig or some twigs.
explain: Read the words around it to work out the meaning. «A stick insect sways like a twig in the wind» tells you a twig is thin and can move gently when the wind blows. «Birds build many kinds of nests: cups of twigs, woven baskets...» tells you that birds use twigs to build their nests.
explain: In the UK, twig can also be an informal verb. «I finally twigged» means «I finally understood». Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «I finally understood» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A twig is a small, thin branch of a tree or bush.
fact: Birds use twigs to build nests, such as cups of twigs.
fact: A twig can also be a bit of a bush or tree that bends and sways in the wind.
fact: In UK informal English, «I finally twigged» means «I finally understood».
fact: In stories, a «snapping twig» can warn that someone is coming.
exercise: «A stick insect sways like a twig in the wind.» What is a twig? | A kind of wind | A bird's song | A large, heavy stone | *A small, thin branch of a tree or bush
exercise: «Birds build many kinds of nests: cups of twigs, woven baskets, mud nests and holes in trees.» Find and copy the word that names what birds use to build cups. | *twigs | baskets | mud | nests
exercise: Priya says, «I finally twigged why the dog kept barking.» What does twigged mean here? | I went to sleep | *I finally understood | I got wet | I broke a branch
test: In a story, «a snapping twig» in the dark might mean what? | It is raining | *Someone is coming | Dinner is ready | The story has ended
test: Which part of a tree is a small, thin branch? | fire | trunk | *twig | nest
exam: Which sentence uses twig as a noun? | He twigged what the teacher meant. | *The bird flew down to a twig. | I finally twigged the answer. | She twigged that we were lost.
